0..73 Comment "// Rust\'s default layout as a program over codes. A type\'s code lists its"
74..151 Comment "// fields\' scalars (structs) or its variants\' fields (enums), and the program"
152..224 Comment "// places them as rustc places a `repr(Rust)` type: `univariant` sorts a"
225..304 Comment "// struct\'s fields by alignment, largest first, its niche toward the start and,"
305..382 Comment "// when that leaves the niche nearer the middle, toward the end; `enumLayout`"
383..460 Comment "// builds the niche-filled and the tagged layouts and keeps the smaller, then"
461..536 Comment "// the one with the larger niche, then the tagged one, a tag widened to the"
537..607 Comment "// smallest first-field alignment (`compiler/rustc_abi/src/layout.rs`:"
608..677 Comment "// `univariant`, `univariant_biased`, `layout_of_enum`). rustc is the"
678..754 Comment "// authority on a Rust type\'s layout, and the program is checked against it:"
755..831 Comment "// each layout below is what `rustc -Zprint-type-sizes` printed for the type"
832..910 Comment "// (nightly 1.98.0, f28ac764c, 2026-06-23, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu), and each"
911..942 Comment "// `runs` re-checks it offline."
943..945 Comment "//"
946..997 Comment "// | type | size | align | fields in memory order |"
998..1026 Comment "// | --- | --- | --- | --- |"
1027..1104 Comment "// | `struct Mixed { a: u8, b: u32, c: u16 }` | 8 | 4 | `b` 0, `c` 4, `a` 6 |"
1105..1181 Comment "// | `struct Wide { a: u8, b: u64, c: u8 }` | 16 | 8 | `b` 0, `a` 8, `c` 9 |"
1182..1244 Comment "// | `struct Small { x: u16, y: u8 }` | 4 | 2 | `x` 0, `y` 2 |"
1245..1325 Comment "// | `struct Flagged { a: u8, b: bool, c: u16 }` | 4 | 2 | `c` 0, `a` 2, `b` 3 |"
1326..1402 Comment "// | `enum MaybeRef { Some(&u32), None }` | 8 | 8 | niche at 0; `Some.0` 0 |"
1403..1479 Comment "// | `enum MaybeFlag { Set(bool), Unset }` | 1 | 1 | niche at 0; `Set.0` 0 |"
1480..1572 Comment "// | `enum Either { Left(u32), Right(u16) }` | 8 | 4 | 2-byte tag; `Left.0` 4, `Right.0` 2 |"
1573..1680 Comment "// | `enum Jagged { Full(u32, bool), Thin(u8) }` | 8 | 4 | 1-byte tag; `Full.1` 1, `Full.0` 4, `Thin.0` 1 |"
1681..1765 Comment "// | `enum ThreeRef { First, Held(&u32), Last }` | 16 | 8 | 8-byte tag; `Held.0` 8 |"
1766..1850 Comment "// | `enum ThreeFlag { First, Held(bool), Last }` | 1 | 1 | niche at 0; `Held.0` 0 |"
1851..1853 Comment "//"
1854..1927 Comment "// Not yet: a field that is itself an aggregate, an array or a zero-sized"
1928..2001 Comment "// type, whose alignment group rustc derives from its size, waits for the"
2002..2079 Comment "// program to run over levitated codes (#2343); a niche beyond `bool`\'s and a"
2080..2151 Comment "// reference\'s (`char`, `NonZero`, an enum\'s own) needs a theory of the"
2152..2228 Comment "// target; `repr` attributes and targets other than x86-64 are not modelled."
